            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Is Sony's console business 'dying'? PS5 prices aren't helping",
            "description": "<p>Wedbush Securities managing director of strategic planning Michael Pachter explains to Yahoo Finance how Sony's (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/SONY\">SONY</a>) gaming console business is struggling, underlining how Playstation 5 prices have seen little reduction under inflation since its launch in November 2020.</p>\n<p>Also catch Michael Pachter's analysis on the <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/why-trump-blocking-netflix-wbd-162609174.html\">bidding wars for Warner Bros. Discovery </a>(<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/WBD\">WBD</a>) and his forecasts for <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/2026-record-within-last-decade-150012966.html\">video game sales in 2026.</a></p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
